     "caption": "The large intestine starts at the cecum (the blind pouch), where the ileum joins it through the ileocecal valve. The worm-like appendix hangs from the cecum. The colon (Col/o, Colon/o) runs up (ascending), across (transverse), down (descending) and through the S-shaped sigmoid colon to the rectum (Rect/o) and anus (An/o).",
